# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Switchboard Server — .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The important line in this file is the `data/` block below. Everything in
# that folder is live household data — every room's Home Assistant
# long-lived access token, the household WiFi password(s), and the shared
# Home Assistant connection — written there by the app itself (the default
# DATA_DIR, when nothing overrides it, is this repo's own data/ folder; see
# lib/store.js). None of it belongs in git, ever. See README.md's
# "Secrets & .gitignore" section before your first commit.

# ---- Runtime data (the important one) --------------------------------------
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# ---- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# ---- Env files (none exist yet, but if one gets added later) ----------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Editor / OS cruft --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Docker build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------
*.tar
